## Decision and status

Proposed replacement for [accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).
The accepted record is preserved, not retroactively edited. Desk approval has not been recorded.
Use the tenant, channel, booking-form version and evidence of mechanism to decide whether reports share a cause.
Do not merge unknown-tenant reports just because their subjects match; establish their context first.

<Callout>
The old subject-only rule and “one issue” incident narrative disagree with their executable views.
Accepted is a workflow status, not proof that guidance is current. The old accepted guidance is stale;
the newer incident narrative is also contradicted by its own table.
</Callout>

## What the export establishes

The source ticket [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) combines two date mechanisms.
That source-system identifier is not a new GitHub issue number.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

**Parser:** the shared parser interprets dates month first, despite the tenant's day-first locale.
App/email reports and booking-v2 form reports fall here. Expected: interpret the tenant's date as intended,
not the month-first swap. Representative source reports: `R-41200`, `R-41201`.

**Hint:** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, prompting month-first input, but its form interprets that input
in the tenant's day-first order. Expected: the hint and interpretation agree. Representative source reports:
`R-41230`, `R-41241`, `R-41251` (copper.studio, alder.physio, pale.harbour).

Public tickets: [parser issue #1](https://github.com/xxrafalekkoo/s01e03_tests/issues/1)
and [hint issue #2](https://github.com/xxrafalekkoo/s01e03_tests/issues/2).
The table's “no ticket of its own” describes the supplied export, not the state of GitHub.

<InvestigationSummary />

Browser locale and `meta.intakeTag` are intake guesses. The tenant directory supplies the actual locale and form version.
All configured tenant locales are day-first according to runtime Intl ordering, not a hand-maintained country list.

## Dedupe by mechanism

Matching subjects can hide different causes: alder.physio form and app reports split despite identical wording;
copper.studio and morrow.tax form reports also split. Different subjects can share a cause:
pale.harbour and alder.physio forms belong together; kettle.books app and email belong together.
These are reproducible classifier cases, not a claim that every similarly worded report has been diagnosed.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Arrival is not merge activity

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The July merge spike reflects backlog consolidation. Reports existed beforehand and continued afterwards.
The latest exported body says the reporter has stopped reporting these but a colleague encouraged this report;
that is a reason not to interpret a quiet queue as recovery. This export cannot establish live service health,
a shipped fix, or the number of unreported failures. The old page's “fix queued” is not delivery evidence.

## Unresolved symptoms and evidence boundary

The desk-noted bodies include a one-day shift, a June-only pattern, an invite arriving before booking,
and different dates in Lisbon and Toronto. Those symptoms deserve follow-up with original timestamps,
timezones, input values and reproduction steps. Tenant/channel classification files them under parser;
it does not prove that the parser explains each body. Do not silently drop them, move them to hint,
or open a separately counted timezone issue without evidence for that mechanism.

Sources: exported `reports-4471.json`, `desk-notes.json`, tenant directory, `causes.ts`, `locales.ts`,
`dedupe-cases.ts` and `QueueTimeline.svelte`. The deterministic `evidence/report-causes.json` maps each
unique source ID to its runtime cause. Tests reconcile it with independent JSON analysis.
Snapshot exported 2026-10-04; this review adds no live production data.

